<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian treasury raises 66 mln dinars at auction.</title>
<headline>Tunisian treasury raises 66 mln dinars at auction.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tunisian Treasury raised 66 million dinars at its weekly auction of treasury bills dated June 24, and repaid maturing paper totalling 42.9 million dinars.</p>
<p>Herewith breakdown of the results:</p>
<p>  Maturity			    Amount	Rate	 Previous</p>
<p>rate - Two-year notes payable</p>
<p>in equal annual tranches</p>
<p>					10 million     6.9375	    6.9375</p>
<p>					51 million     7.0000	    7.0000</p>
<p>- Two-year note payable at maturity</p>
<p>					 5 million     7.0000	    6.8750</p>
<p>Banks bid for 180 million dinars for two, three and</p>
<p>five-year paper at between 6.9375 and 8.0625 percent.</p>
<p>(one $=1.09 dinar)</p>
<p>--Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
</text>
